{
  "number": 20,
  "meaning": "The number 20 symbolizes a period of waiting, testing, and maturity – marking the transition to full responsibility.",
  "description": "Jacob waited 20 years while serving Laban before he was freed (Genesis 31:38–41), and the Israelites were oppressed for 20 years under Jabin, king of Canaan, before Deborah and Barak delivered them (Judges 4:3). In Jewish tradition, 20 years was considered the age of maturity and responsibility, when men from 20 years old and upward were mustered for military service (Numbers 1:3). Samson judged Israel for 20 years (Judges 15:20), and it took 20 years to complete the building of Solomon's temple and royal palace (1 Kings 9:10). The number is thus linked to a transition from imperfection to full responsibility and deliverance after a period of trials.",
